    "created_at": "2016-03-17T13:24:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-17T13:24:54Z",
    "body": "Here the behavior we implemented in FF to make FormData compatible with the current use of this API on the web:\n\n```\nvar f = document.createElement(\"form\");\nf.innerHTML = \"<input type=file name=test>\";\nvar fd = new FormData(f);\nconsole.log(fd.get(\"test\"));\n```\n\nWe see an empty string. But when we use it with XHR (or in a normal form submission):\n\n```\nvar f = document.createElement(\"form\"); \nf.setAttribute(\"enctype\", \"multipart/form-data\");\nf.innerHTML = \"<input type=file name=test>\";\nvar fd = new FormData(f);\nvar xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();\nxhr.open(\"POST\", window.location.href, true);\nxhr.send(fd);\n```\n\nWe send this:\n\n```\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"test\"; filename=\"\"\nContent-Type: application/octet-stream\n```\n\nWould be nice if the spec follows this behavior. Anything else breaks important websites.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
